	(footprint "dreams_v3:RaspberryPi_5_GPIO_Socket_2x20"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "2f5bbf34-edae-4d4e-9b17-94f89a60773b")
		(at 117.8323 11.3)
		(descr "Raspberry Pi 5 40-pin GPIO socket (female 2x20, 2.54mm) plus 4 non-plated M3 mounting holes 49 x 58 mm apart, the Pi mounting pattern. MOUNTING: Pi sits ABOVE the carrier, upside down, fan/header side facing the PCB, so its male pins come down into this socket. FIXED 2026-08-05: the V2 board this came from had the odd/even columns transposed (pad N landed on Pi pin N-+1), which caused repeated wiring problems. Columns are now swapped so pad N = Pi pin N. VERIFY pin 1 against the physical Pi before fab. A PIN1 silkscreen marker sits beside pad 1.")
		(tags "Through hole socket strip THT 2x20 2.54mm double row")
